# What EAS uploads. Read INSTEAD of .gitignore, not in addition to it — so this
# file has to repeat everything .gitignore excludes, and its one deliberate
# difference is the reason it exists.
#
# THE DIFFERENCE: `modules/cal-ffi/android/src/main/jniLibs/` is NOT excluded
# here. Those are the cargo-ndk builds of libcal_ffi.so, gitignored because they
# are regenerable build output that has no business in version control. Without
# this file EAS applied that same rule to its upload and shipped an app with no
# native library at all — installable, launching, and dead at the first bridge
# call:
#
#     UnsatisfiedLinkError: dlopen failed: library "libcal_ffi.so" not found
#
# Force-adding them to git did not help, and could not: EAS reads the ignore
# rules, not the index. The CI workflow's "ephemeral commit" step was written on
# that assumption and fixed nothing, because the commit was never the mechanism
# that mattered.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Google Play service-account key (written from a CI secret; never upload)
/google-service-account.json

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated native projects. EAS runs prebuild itself, and uploading a stale
# local android/ directory is how a build ends up packaging months-old outputs.
/ios
/android

# Gradle build output for local native modules — regenerable, and large.
/modules/*/android/build/
/modules/*/android/.cxx/
/modules/*/android/.gradle/
